the nominees for Best Motion Picture are  the Curious Case of Benjamin Button  Kathleen Kennedy Frank Marshall and Seon  Chafin producers frost/nixon Brian  Grazer Ron Howard and Eric Felner  producers milk dan jinx and Bruce Cohen  producers the reader Anthony Minghella  Sydney [ __ ] Donna Jia T and Redman  Morris producers Slumdog Millionaire  Christian Coulson producer the Oscar  goes to Slumdog Millionaire  [Applause]  [Music]  thank you so much to the Academy as as  you can see our film was a collaboration  between hundreds of people and I'm so  happy that so many of them could be with  us here tonight to share this moment  together we've been on an extraordinary  an extraordinary journey when we started  out we had no stars we had no power or  muscle we didn't have enough money  really to do what we wanted to do but  what we had was a script that inspired  mad love in everyone who read it we had  a genius for a director we had a cast  and a crew who were unwavering in their  commitment and whose talents are up on  the screen for all of you to see we had  partners in film four and Salladhor in  pathway and Fox Searchlight who had the  courage to support us and we had a  shared love for the extraordinary city  of Mumbai where we made the movie most  of all we had passion and we had belief  in our film shows that if you have those  two things truly anything is possible i  want to thank on a personal note my mum  and my dad for all their love and  support over the years i want to thank  my girl Saskia Mulder who's my partner  in crime and the light in my life and I  want to thank all of you very much  indeed thanks  [Applause]
 

